Subject: Dedupe 490 group numbers without the preceding:: axis

ConvSpec-Process6-Series.xsl builds a result tree fragment holding one
bf:title, bf:identifiedBy and bf:seriesEnumeration per group of 490 subfields,
each tagged with a groupNum, then takes the distinct group numbers to decide
how many bf:Relation nodes to emit. The distinct-values idiom it uses asks,
from an attribute node, for preceding::bf:*/@groupNum.

libxslt gets that axis wrong over a node-set made with exsl:node-set: it omits
the preceding sibling element itself while including that sibling's
descendants. The groupNum being compared against is therefore never in the
node-set, nothing is filtered, and a 490 whose fragment has more than one
child -- any 490 with a $v or a $x alongside its $a -- yields one identical
bf:Relation per child. Downstream that is a work with two indistinguishable
bf:relation values.

An eight-line reproducer, with an <a n="1"><deep/></a> and a <b n="1"/> as
siblings in a fragment, asking for preceding::* from the @n on b:

  libxslt  [deep]     <- wrong, a is missing
  Saxon    [a deep]

On a plain source document both processors agree and both are right, so this
only shows up for fragments, and only on libxslt. Saxon is what upstream
develops and runs CI against, which is why the code is correct there and
lcnetdev has not seen it.

Comparing preceding-sibling::*/@groupNum from the element instead of
preceding::bf:*/@groupNum from the attribute avoids the axis entirely.
Verified against Saxon HE 12.4 and libxslt 1.1.35 over the upstream test data:
Saxon output is unchanged byte for byte, and libxslt now agrees with Saxon
exactly where it previously emitted duplicates.

Upstream status: not yet reported to lcnetdev/marc2bibframe2. The libxslt axis
bug is not yet reported either.
Origin: https://github.com/blue-core-lod/marc-bibframe/issues/2

diff --git a/src/marc_bibframe/xsl/ConvSpec-Process6-Series.xsl b/src/marc_bibframe/xsl/ConvSpec-Process6-Series.xsl
index 7c5ee20..57d05ed 100644
--- a/src/marc_bibframe/xsl/ConvSpec-Process6-Series.xsl
+++ b/src/marc_bibframe/xsl/ConvSpec-Process6-Series.xsl
@@ -63,7 +63,7 @@
     
     <!-- Find the group numbers. -->
     <xsl:variable name="tThisDF" select="."/>
-      <xsl:variable name="tGroupNums" select="$grouped490Info//@groupNum[not(.=preceding::bf:*/@groupNum[1])]" />
+      <xsl:variable name="tGroupNums" select="$grouped490Info/*[not(@groupNum = preceding-sibling::*/@groupNum)]/@groupNum" />
       <xsl:for-each select="$tGroupNums">
         <xsl:variable name="tGNum" select="."/>    
         <bf:relation>
